just a few days ago these people were  fleeing the war in ukraine now they are  arriving in berlin  after a journey which has lasted many  hours  the chaos of the last week has separated  many from their families and brought  them to a city which is welcoming them  as refugees  for some the experience has been  overwhelming  i was on the train from kiev  when the bomb started to fall  i can still hear the explosions in my  ears now  the whole train was shaking  we have no plan  i  i don't just  we run we run  and don't know what to do  i want to work  and  send money in ukraine  to help the army and  ukraine  and for the many still stuck in the war  zone there are people here trying to  help them  assembling packages of essential  supplies as at this center in potsdam  or in berlin where some people have  initiated their own donation campaign  collecting food water and clothing which  can then be taken on by ukrainian truck  drivers  you come here we balance  they come here we load them up and they  go to ukraine and in ukraine the  volunteers will then receive them and  then distribute the stuff to the needed  towns or villages wherever the help is  needed  for the established charities here the  need is clear  german red cross officials say their  ukrainian colleagues need is great  it's barely a week since russia invaded  ukraine and these are some of the first  people to make it all the way here as  refugees there but maybe many many more  dominic kane al jazeera at berlin's main  train station
 

